
AXE - Program compression utility - v2.2 
Copyright 1987-1989 System Enhancement Associates

Usage:  axe <source> [<backup>]  [-n] [-c<bytes>] [-s<clusters>] [-o<bytes>]

  <source> is the program to compress
  <backup> is the optional backup program name

    -n     deletes the backup (CAUTION - see manual)
    -c     sets the cluster size in bytes
    -s     sets the minimum number of clusters to save
    -o     sets the overlay warning size in bytes
    -f     forces the compression (ignore warnings)

